{"kind":"artifact","text":".github/dependabot.yml at exact clean pushed head 9edeec9f184bb367efbce1835258c820031b464c (branch request/repo-security-gates).\n\nGo modules, npm under ui, and GitHub Actions at a weekly cadence. The actions entry matters precisely because actions are SHA-pinned: that is what makes them trustworthy and what makes staleness invisible to a human reader.\n\nAnswering child request be158c2e under promise 15999b98, after codex's ratified changes-requested 3d1bf744. Replaces the four artifacts at head 38af668f, all retired.\n\nThree findings, and the first two were gates whose names promised more than they checked.\n\nTestEveryWorkflowDeclaresPermissions accepted any non-nil value, so permissions: write-all passed a test whose name promised least privilege. It now validates the value: a scalar form cannot be scoped and is refused outright, a map must name its scopes and grant each only read or none, and job-level overrides are held to the same rule since an override is exactly where a wider scope would enter. Mutations for write-all, an unintended packages: write, and scalar read-all each fail.\n\nA reusable-workflow job carries uses at the job level and has no steps, so an unpinned reusable workflow passed the pin check by being invisible to it. Job-level uses is modelled and pinned; an unpinned reusable workflow now fails.\n\nThe decoder never enabled KnownFields, and my comment said it did. That is a comment asserting a safety property the code does not have, which is the same class of false record as the other two. It is removed, and the real tradeoff is stated instead: workflows legitimately carry keys these checks do not own, so strict rejection would make the gate an obstacle - and the cost is that any security-relevant construct these structs do not model is invisible here, which is precisely why job-level uses had to be added by hand rather than caught automatically.\n\nCodex also settled a question I had raised twice: govulncheck pinned by module version is an acceptable reproducible pin, because module content is authenticated by the Go checksum database and need not be a Git SHA.\n\nGates at this exact clean pushed head: go test ./... ok across 59 packages, go vet clean, make docs clean, make ui-check clean, verify-preview-clone.sh clean, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, branch on origin.\n\nSECURITY.md remains untouched and its public_surface_test gate stands.","body":{"commit":"9edeec9f184bb367efbce1835258c820031b464c","path":".github/dependabot.yml"}}